CAT = "phrebOwnership"; SEG = "OWN"
Q = [
('Under the Civil Code, lands, buildings and roads, and constructions of all kinds adhered to the soil, are classified as:',
 'Immovable property', ['Movable property', 'Fungible property', 'Consumable property'],
 'Article 415 of the Civil Code lists lands, buildings, roads and constructions adhered to the soil as immovable property, the subject of real estate service.'),
("An owner's right to receive the fruits of his land, such as rentals or harvests, is called:",
 'Jus fruendi', ['Jus utendi', 'Jus disponendi', 'Jus vindicandi'],
 'Ownership includes the right to use (jus utendi), to enjoy the fruits (jus fruendi), to dispose (jus disponendi) and to recover (jus vindicandi). Fruits belong to the owner by right of accession.'),
("Soil gradually deposited by a river's current on land bordering the river belongs to:",
 'The owner of the bank', ['The State', 'The municipality', 'The first person to fence it'],
 'Under Article 457, accretion that lands on the banks of rivers gradually receive from the current belongs to the owners of the land along the banks (alluvion).'),
("Ramon builds a house in good faith on Lita's lot, believing it is his. Under Article 448, Lita may choose to:",
 'Buy the house or sell the land', ['Demolish it at no cost', 'Take the house for free', "Order the house demolished at the builder's cost"],
 'When a builder acted in good faith, the landowner may appropriate the building after paying indemnity, or oblige the builder to pay the price of the land (unless the land is considerably worth more).'),
('Three siblings inherit a lot in undivided shares. Their relationship over the lot is:',
 'Co-ownership', ['Usufruct', 'Easement', 'Conjugal partnership'],
 'Co-ownership exists when ownership of an undivided thing belongs to different persons (Article 484). Each co-owner holds an ideal share, not a specific portion.'),
('Under Article 494, any co-owner of an undivided lot may, at any time:',
 'Demand partition', ['Sell the entire lot alone', 'Bar the others from using it', 'Lease it to anyone for 25 years'],
 'No co-owner is obliged to remain in the co-ownership; each may demand partition of the thing owned in common at any time, subject to a valid agreement to keep it undivided.'),
('A widow is given the right to live in and collect rentals from a building for life, while her children own it. Her right is:',
 'Usufruct', ['Easement', 'Ownership in fee', 'Antichresis'],
 'Usufruct gives the right to enjoy the property of another with the obligation of preserving its form and substance (Article 562). The children keep naked ownership.'),
('A real right over an immovable that benefits another immovable belonging to a different owner is a:',
 'Predial servitude', ['Personal servitude', 'Mortgage', 'Usufruct'],
 'An easement or servitude is an encumbrance imposed on an immovable for the benefit of another immovable belonging to a different owner (Article 613). It is predial because it attaches to land.'),
('The owner of an enclosed lot with no adequate outlet to a public road may demand a right of way:',
 'On payment of indemnity', ['Free of any charge', 'Only from the city', 'Only if the neighbor freely agrees'],
 'Article 649 grants a compulsory easement of right of way to the owner of an isolated estate, after payment of the proper indemnity.'),
('When a compulsory right of way is set up, it must be at the point:',
 'Least prejudicial to the servient estate', ['Most convenient for any visitor', 'Chosen freely by the owner of the enclosed lot', 'Nearest the barangay hall'],
 'Article 650 requires the right of way to be established at the point least prejudicial to the servient estate and, as far as consistent with that rule, where the distance to the road is shortest.'),
('Ownership acquired by possession in the concept of owner, public, peaceful and uninterrupted, for the period set by law, is acquired by:',
 'Acquisitive prescription', ['Extinctive prescription', 'Accretion', 'Intestate succession by heirs'],
 'Acquisitive prescription is a mode of acquiring ownership through possession for the time fixed by law. Note that it does not run against land registered under the Torrens system.'),
('Ordinary acquisitive prescription of an immovable requires possession in good faith and with just title for:',
 'Ten years', ['Four years', 'Thirty years', 'Fifty years'],
 'Article 1134 sets ten years for ordinary prescription of immovables (good faith and just title). Extraordinary prescription without them takes thirty years (Article 1137).'),
('Under the 1987 Constitution, private lands may be transferred, except by hereditary succession, only to:',
 'Those qualified to hold public lands', ['Any resident foreigner', 'Foreign banks', 'Any foreign investor who registers with the BOI'],
 'Article XII, Section 7 limits transfers of private lands, save hereditary succession, to individuals, corporations or associations qualified to acquire or hold lands of the public domain.'),
('A corporation may own private land in the Philippines if Filipino citizens own at least:',
 '60% of its capital', ['51% of its capital', '40% of its capital', '75% of its capital'],
 'Article XII, Section 7 of the Constitution allows private land to pass only to those qualified to hold public land, and corporations qualify only if at least 60% of their capital is Filipino-owned, the same line R.A. 7042 uses for a Philippine national.'),
('Which of these is a personal servitude rather than a predial one?',
 'Usufruct', ['Right of way', 'Drainage of waters', 'Light and view'],
 'Personal servitudes, like usufruct, are constituted in favor of a person, not a piece of land. Right of way, drainage and light and view benefit a dominant estate.'),
('Property for public use, such as roads, canals and rivers, belongs to the State and is:',
 'Outside the commerce of man', ['Open to private registration', 'Subject to prescription', 'Sellable by the LGU'],
 'Property of public dominion is outside the commerce of man: it cannot be sold, registered in private names, or acquired by prescription while it remains for public use.'),
]
